  <policies id="pol-checkout" name="Atomic basket allocation" description="Check the complete basket and current quoted price revisions. Reserve every line and create order/payment state together or change nothing; no negative availability." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="Check the complete basket and current quoted price revisions. Reserve every line and create order/payment state together or change nothing; no negative availability." policyType="GUARD" guards="cmd-checkout" triggeredBy="" emitsCommands="" decisionTable="dt-checkout" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-payment" name="Guarded payment application" description="Only authenticated provider facts or trusted reconciliation observations may change payment state. Verify order/session association, one capture reference per order, amount, currency, fact identity, and provider occurrence time. A first matching capture pays an AWAITING_PAYMENT order only when both provider capturedAt and processing time are strictly before expiresAt. Commit PAID, payment CAPTURED and HELD-to-COMMITTED together. A capture first learned at/after the deadline or after cancellation/expiry creates one full refund obligation; never reopen that order. A repeated already-applied capture is a no-op even after the deadline. Stale unpaid/decline facts cannot downgrade a capture. Invalid, conflicting, or mismatched facts are quarantined for staff inspection with no order/stock mutation. Unknown or erased order references are rejected without retaining the supplied personal or financial references; only an anonymous rejection count may remain. Quarantine applies to verifiable existing retained orders. At now &gt;= expiresAt, trusted due processing shall change each still-AWAITING_PAYMENT order to EXPIRED and release every HELD line atomically, completing within sixty seconds. A verified definitive unpaid/declined result before expiry instead changes an awaiting order to CANCELLED and releases its holds. Already-paid orders are never expired. Unknown payment outcomes remain under reconciliation, and a later discovered capture follows the refund rule." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="Only authenticated provider facts or trusted reconciliation observations may change payment state. Verify order/session association, one capture reference per order, amount, currency, fact identity, and provider occurrence time. A first matching capture pays an AWAITING_PAYMENT order only when both provider capturedAt and processing time are strictly before expiresAt. Commit PAID, payment CAPTURED and HELD-to-COMMITTED together. A capture first learned at/after the deadline or after cancellation/expiry creates one full refund obligation; never reopen that order. A repeated already-applied capture is a no-op even after the deadline. Stale unpaid/decline facts cannot downgrade a capture. Invalid, conflicting, or mismatched facts are quarantined for staff inspection with no order/stock mutation. Unknown or erased order references are rejected without retaining the supplied personal or financial references; only an anonymous rejection count may remain. Quarantine applies to verifiable existing retained orders. At now &gt;= expiresAt, trusted due processing shall change each still-AWAITING_PAYMENT order to EXPIRED and release every HELD line atomically, completing within sixty seconds. A verified definitive unpaid/declined result before expiry instead changes an awaiting order to CANCELLED and releases its holds. Already-paid orders are never expired. Unknown payment outcomes remain under reconciliation, and a later discovered capture follows the refund rule." policyType="GUARD" guards="cmd-payment" triggeredBy="" emitsCommands="" decisionTable="dt-payment" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-expiry" name="Unpaid hold expiry" description="At now &gt;= expiresAt, trusted due processing shall change each still-AWAITING_PAYMENT order to EXPIRED and release every HELD line atomically, completing within sixty seconds. A verified definitive unpaid/declined result before expiry instead changes an awaiting order to CANCELLED and releases its holds. Already-paid orders are never expired. Unknown payment outcomes remain under reconciliation, and a later discovered capture follows the refund rule." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="At now &gt;= expiresAt, trusted due processing shall change each still-AWAITING_PAYMENT order to EXPIRED and release every HELD line atomically, completing within sixty seconds. A verified definitive unpaid/declined result before expiry instead changes an awaiting order to CANCELLED and releases its holds. Already-paid orders are never expired. Unknown payment outcomes remain under reconciliation, and a later discovered capture follows the refund rule." policyType="GUARD" guards="cmd-expire" triggeredBy="" emitsCommands="" decisionTable="" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-cancel" name="Cancellation and readiness exclusion" description="A customer may cancel only their own AWAITING_PAYMENT or PAID order. Cancellation of an awaiting order before its deadline produces CANCELLED and releases holds; at/after the deadline it is processed as EXPIRED. Cancellation of PAID atomically produces CANCELLED, releases committed stock, and records REFUND_PENDING with a full-refund obligation. READY and COLLECTED orders cannot be cancelled. Repeating a completed cancellation is harmless. If staff readiness races cancellation, exactly one eligible transition wins." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="A customer may cancel only their own AWAITING_PAYMENT or PAID order. Cancellation of an awaiting order before its deadline produces CANCELLED and releases holds; at/after the deadline it is processed as EXPIRED. Cancellation of PAID atomically produces CANCELLED, releases committed stock, and records REFUND_PENDING with a full-refund obligation. READY and COLLECTED orders cannot be cancelled. Repeating a completed cancellation is harmless. If staff readiness races cancellation, exactly one eligible transition wins." policyType="GUARD" guards="cmd-cancel cmd-ready" triggeredBy="" emitsCommands="" decisionTable="" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-reconcile" name="Apply reconciled provider fact" description="A verified ledger observation must use the same association, amount, deadline, idempotency and monotonic payment guards as callbacks." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="A verified ledger observation must use the same association, amount, deadline, idempotency and monotonic payment guards as callbacks." policyType="REACTION" guards="" triggeredBy="evt-payment-observed" emitsCommands="cmd-payment" decisionTable="" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-refund" name="Durable full refund processing" description="Refunds are full amount only, against the verified capture, using one immutable provider refund key per capture. Durable refund obligations arise from paid cancellation or late capture. Trusted processing submits immediately, then retries eligible failures after at least one minute and five minutes, within sixty seconds of each due time, with at most three automatic submission attempts. A timeout uses lookup/reconciliation and the same key, never a new refund. Verified completion changes payment to REFUNDED and records refundedAt. After automatic exhaustion keep REFUND_PENDING with needsAttention=true; staff may retry the same obligation/key, without changing order or stock. Provider acceptance of a refund request alone is not refund completion." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="Refunds are full amount only, against the verified capture, using one immutable provider refund key per capture. Durable refund obligations arise from paid cancellation or late capture. Trusted processing submits immediately, then retries eligible failures after at least one minute and five minutes, within sixty seconds of each due time, with at most three automatic submission attempts. A timeout uses lookup/reconciliation and the same key, never a new refund. Verified completion changes payment to REFUNDED and records refundedAt. After automatic exhaustion keep REFUND_PENDING with needsAttention=true; staff may retry the same obligation/key, without changing order or stock. Provider acceptance of a refund request alone is not refund completion." policyType="REACTION" guards="" triggeredBy="evt-refund-required evt-refund-attempt" emitsCommands="cmd-refund" decisionTable="" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-notice" name="Notice preparation and relevance" description="Committed paid, cancelled, ready, and refund-completed facts shall create one durable notice intent per fact/order/kind. Include order reference, resulting status, authoritative amount when relevant, and store pickup details for readiness. Deduplicate redelivered facts. Before every send, suppress obsolete notices: PAID requires order PAID, READY requires READY, CANCELLED requires CANCELLED, REFUNDED requires payment REFUNDED. Each kind also requires unexpired retention. Provider acceptance means accepted for email delivery, not arrival in an inbox. Retry failures after one and five minutes, three total attempts maximum; exhausted failures remain visible to staff and never change order/payment/stock." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="Committed paid, cancelled, ready, and refund-completed facts shall create one durable notice intent per fact/order/kind. Include order reference, resulting status, authoritative amount when relevant, and store pickup details for readiness. Deduplicate redelivered facts. Before every send, suppress obsolete notices: PAID requires order PAID, READY requires READY, CANCELLED requires CANCELLED, REFUNDED requires payment REFUNDED. Each kind also requires unexpired retention. Provider acceptance means accepted for email delivery, not arrival in an inbox. Retry failures after one and five minutes, three total attempts maximum; exhausted failures remain visible to staff and never change order/payment/stock." policyType="REACTION" guards="" triggeredBy="evt-order-paid evt-order-cancelled evt-refund-completed evt-order-ready" emitsCommands="cmd-prepare-notice" decisionTable="" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-delivery" name="Notice delivery and bounded retry" description="Deliver newly prepared notices and relevant failed notices under R14 retry limits. Suppressed or exhausted outcomes never schedule another automatic attempt." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="Deliver newly prepared notices and relevant failed notices under R14 retry limits. Suppressed or exhausted outcomes never schedule another automatic attempt." policyType="REACTION" guards="" triggeredBy="evt-notice-prepared evt-notice-outcome" emitsCommands="cmd-deliver-notice" decisionTable="" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <policies id="pol-retention" name="Erase settled terminal orders" description="Use only customer identifier, display name, verified email, order history and provider transaction references needed for this scenario; no card data, shipping address, or marketing profile is stored. For CANCELLED, EXPIRED or COLLECTED orders, erase identifying orders/lines/payment/notice/audit/fact/request-key records within twenty-four hours after the later of terminal order time plus thirty days and financial settlement time. Financial settlement means verified captured payment for a collected order, definitive unpaid closure, or verified full refund for a cancelled/expired charged order. Pending/unresolved refunds are not erased and remain visible to staff. Retain only anonymous sales/refund totals, product data, and a non-identifying erasure receipt that cannot link back to a person/order/provider reference. Stop late facts from recreating erased personal records." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:Policy" naturalLanguageRule="Use only customer identifier, display name, verified email, order history and provider transaction references needed for this scenario; no card data, shipping address, or marketing profile is stored. For CANCELLED, EXPIRED or COLLECTED orders, erase identifying orders/lines/payment/notice/audit/fact/request-key records within twenty-four hours after the later of terminal order time plus thirty days and financial settlement time. Financial settlement means verified captured payment for a collected order, definitive unpaid closure, or verified full refund for a cancelled/expired charged order. Pending/unresolved refunds are not erased and remain visible to staff. Retain only anonymous sales/refund totals, product data, and a non-identifying erasure receipt that cannot link back to a person/order/provider reference. Stop late facts from recreating erased personal records." policyType="GUARD" guards="cmd-purge" triggeredBy="" emitsCommands="" decisionTable="" enforcementStrength="MANDATORY" violationSeverity="ERROR" auditRequired="true" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false" />
  <decisionTables id="dt-checkout" name="Ordered checkout decisions" description="Evaluate the first matching row; exact replay is resolved before any new business change." sourceReference="model-guide.md" xsi:type="cimprocess:DecisionTable" hitPolicy="FIRST" complete="false" defaultOutcome="Flag unmatched conflicting/invalid state for staff; preserve stock and monetary state." inputs="info-basket info-available info-price info-price-revision info-operation-key" outputs="info-order-state info-expires info-order-total" generatedByTransformation="false" manuallyMaintained="false">
